EXT. LIFEBOAT - OPEN SEA - DUSK

Gray swells. A battered lifeboat rides low. A torn canvas sail sags from a broken oar.

Four survivors huddle on the thwarts. CAPTAIN HILDEGARD VOSBERG (60s, oilskins) clutches the tiller, the ship's cook BAXTER NNAMDI (40s) bails with a tin cup while the stewardess ISOLDE FAIRWEATHER (30s) rations the last biscuit into crumbs, and the cabin boy JASPER LOCKWOOD (12) leans against her, shivering.

HILDEGARD
Eyes on the horizon.

BAXTER
There's nothing out there, Captain.

ISOLDE
There's always something.

JASPER
Is that a bird?

BAXTER
It's a gull. Gulls mean land.

HILDEGARD
Or a storm.

They scan the sky. A speck wheels and vanishes. The wind drops. The boat creaks. In the silence, a distant drone grows, faint, mechanical.

A small seaplane skims out of the clouds, banking low over the water. PILOT MARCEL DUVALIER (30s, leather helmet) leans from the open cockpit, waving a red flag.

ISOLDE
Oh, thank God.

JASPER
They see us!

PILOT
(shouting over the engine)
Hold your positions! I'm dropping a line!

HILDEGARD
(softly)
Stay seated. All of you.

Nobody moves. Baxter lets the cup slip into the sea.
